# Kitty6 renderer mods: rules of our own, read by crates/victory-gpu/src/kitty6.rs.
# A rule names a translated shader by its runtime hash (as the log and
# `victory replay --timing detailed` print it) and says what to do with the
# draws and dispatches that use it. Nothing of the title is in this file.
#
#   <16 hex digits> skip              never run (joins foxhound's VICTORY_LEAVE_OUT)
#   <16 hex digits> every <n>         run in one frame of n (results stay in place between)
#   <16 hex digits> every <n> at <k>  ... in frames whose number % n == k
#
# scripts\kitty6.ps1 passes every mods\*.k6mod unless -NoMods.

# 02384a60fda6f2d0: the decal heap's defragmentation, one 1x1x1 compute
# dispatch of ~11 ms a frame on NVIDIA. Foxhound leaves it out by default
# (VICTORY_LEAVE_OUT in scripts\play-foxhound.ps1), which wins over any rule
# here. On the old base we ran it every 4th frame instead; to try that here,
# take it out of VICTORY_LEAVE_OUT (kitty6.ps1 -More @{VICTORY_LEAVE_OUT='731a39171b568298'})
# and uncomment:
# 02384a60fda6f2d0 every 4
